  "body": "**Stacked on #573** (#557, part axes by edge or two points). Review only this PR's own commit, `04d8f749`.\n\n**P2 (#664, found in M5's review of #573):** an armed Setups-page pick stayed armed after leaving the page. Edge, vertex and face clicks on an operation page then fed the hidden setup draft instead of the operation's geometry.\n\n## What changed (ephemeral view state, no command)\n- **One sweep.** `pages::properties` clears the \"rows drawn\" markers (`axis_rows_shown`, the new `State::setup_pick_rows`) and draws the page. It then calls `axis_pick::disarm_hidden`, which stops every armed axis or plane pick whose setup rows weren't drawn this frame.\n  - That covers a page or tab change, opening an operation, closing the section, and another setup's page.\n  - The axis and plane rows record their setup each frame they are drawn.\n- **The plane draft is paused, not dropped.** `PlanePick` gains `picking`, `pause()` and `collecting()`.\n  - Re-arming resumes it with the face kept, and on return the row shows the picked face and Apply while disarmed.\n  - The row's own \"Stop picking\" still drops the draft.\n- **Click routing:** `interact.rs`, `vertex_pick.rs` and `hint_stray` ask `plane_pick::collecting`. The plane outlines draw only while collecting, the same as the axis draft.\n- **Decision record:** `docs/decisions/664-disarm-setup-picks.md` (one sweep rather than per-navigation resets; pause rather than drop).\n\n## How tested\n- **New `tests/setup_picks_disarm.rs` (headless, real clicks).** Each test arms the pick from its row and picks once, then switches to the Contour1 operation page and clicks the same pixel: Contour1 gets the pick and the setup draft is unchanged. Back on the setup page, the pick is disarmed and kept.\n  - `an_axis_edge_pick_disarms_when_its_page_is_left`\n  - `an_axis_two_points_pick_disarms_when_its_page_is_left`\n  - `a_plane_face_pick_disarms_when_its_page_is_left` (re-arming resumes with the face)\n  - With the sweep commented out, all three fail.\n- **Updated:** `plane_face_pick`'s existing test armed the plane pick while the operation page was showing, which was the bug. It now opens the setup page first.\n- **Gate:**\n  - ui lib 389 pass. The 1 failure is the known no-GPU `headless_run_succeeds` in the agent sandbox;\n  - boundary_picks, edge_loop_pick, operations, axis_align, axis_direction, plane_align(_edges) and setup_align pass;\n  - clippy is clean. No snapshot PNGs changed.\n\nChangelog: Setups page: an armed axis (by Edge / Two points) or lay-on-plane pick stops collecting when its page is left, so clicks on an operation page reach that operation; the picks stay and show disarmed on return (#664)\n\nFixes #664\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
